both regions."], "text": "Rules for life. Customary law provided a basis for community rules. These rules help us understand local community life. Traditional practices. Customs were practised according to local traditions. Traditions were not necessarily identical between different communities. Inheritance. Practices were passed down through generations. Younger generations learnt this heritage from their elders. Beliefs. Customary law was linked to each community’s beliefs. This relationship concerns the particular communities being described. Diversity. Each community had its own context and heritage. One community does not represent everyone in both regions."}